{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"formation/text\",\"value_json\":\"The current graph 学 is arranged ⿳⺍冖子: ⺍ and 冖 form an upper assembly above 子. This visible split does not settle how traditional 學 was first constructed. One account interprets oracle-bone forms as 𦥑 (two hands) with 五 and 六, while allowing that 爻 may supply a sound cue in some forms. Separate proposals describe associative forms involving 林 + 冖; phonosemantic forms with 爻 as sound and 冖 as the other element; a rare, unidentified element read jù and depicted as hands or claws; and a distinct construction grouping two 臼 forms with 冖 and a following unidentified graphic unit assigned the sound role. The two 臼 shapes may be reduced to person-like forms; this reduction does not apply to 冖. The rare jù account is separate from the two-臼 proposal. These are competing interpretations, not a settled reconstruction. One source also proposes learning and emulation as 學’s original meaning, but the proposal is unsettled. The modern simplified shape does not establish the ancient structure.\"},{\"path\":\"formation/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref021\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref073\\\",\\\"ref080\\\",\\\"ref101\\\",\\\"ref105\\\",\\\"ref113\\\",\\\"ref117\\\",\\\"ref118\\\",\\\"ref125\\\",\\\"ref126\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"uncertainties/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The early construction accounts remain distinct. One interprets some forms as 𦥑 (two hands) with tally-like elements 五 and 六, while allowing that 爻 may supply a sound cue in some forms. Other proposals describe associative forms involving 林 + 冖; phonosemantic forms with 爻 as sound and 冖 as the other element; a separate, unusual element read jù and depicted as hands or claws; and a distinct construction grouping two 臼 forms with 冖 and a following unidentified graphic unit assigned the sound role. The two 臼 shapes may be reduced to person-like forms; this does not apply to 冖, and the rare jù element is not identified as 臼. These proposals do not establish one construction for every early form. The claim that 學’s original meaning was learning and emulation is a proposal, not an established conclusion.\"},{\"path\":\"uncertainties/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref016\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref080\\\",\\\"ref101\\\",\\\"ref105\\\",\\\"ref113\\\",\\\"ref117\\\",\\\"ref118\\\",\\\"ref125\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref073\\\",\\\"ref060\\\",\\\"ref057\\\",\\\"ref070\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref073\\\",\\\"ref021\\\",\\\"ref057\\\",\\\"ref070\\\",\\\"ref126\\\"]\"}]}"}}
